WEBVTT

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.270
One-set match.

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.530
Alex to serve.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.030
<i>My first match in America.</i>

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.280
<i>A match with a pro...</i>

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.580
<i>So heavy!</i>

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.190
15-love.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.840
<i>The ball's weight is totally different...</i>

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.600
<i>This is what a pro is like...</i>

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.090
No!

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:36.890
Out!

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:38.430
15-all.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:42.710
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.940
<i>I need to get used to this ball, and fast.</i>

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:48.610
<i>But... what is this?</i>

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.390
<i>Something feels off.</i>

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.780
30-15.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.780
<i>It's not just the weight of the ball...</i>

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:55.950
<i>Something is different.</i>

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:00.870
<i>This rhythm is hard to keep up with.</i>

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.200
<i>Is this what tennis is like at the world level?</i>

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.660
Alex! That shot was great!

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.470
<i>Right now, I'm...</i>

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.420
<i>fighting against the world!</i>

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.780
That's it!

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.890
Game: Alex. 3-0.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.860
<i>I already knew tennis would 
be different over here.</i>

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.380
<i>Now I need to analyze 
what the difference is!</i>

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.240
<i>Mike?</i>

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:07.240
<i>All right.</i>

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:08.770
<i>Time to get started.</i>

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:18.280
The World and the Wall

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.760
Day 1

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.040
We're here!

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.560
This is the Florida Tennis Academy!

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.560
The campus has exchange student dorms, 
restaurants, shops, and even a pool.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:37.820
<i>Amazing...</i>

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.320
<i>It's like a town that's made for tennis!</i>

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.020
What do you think, Ei-chan?

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:44.670
It hasn't quite hit me yet.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:47.450
To think I'm going to get to 
live here and play tennis...

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:52.460
Hey, Marcia!

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:56.460
Hi, Mike.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.730
<i>Wow, she's beautiful...</i>

00:03:58.730 --> 00:03:59.590
Ei-chan!

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.080
Come here, come here!

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:04.760
I'm Marcia.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.590
Uh...

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.380
I'm M-Maruo Eiichiro.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:10.350
Nice to meet you.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:11.840
Eichiro?

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.980
Nice to meet you, too.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.480
He's a seventeen-year-old exchange 
student who's aiming for the pros.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.630
He'll be here for two weeks.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:22.410
He just flew in from Japan, 
so he's a little jet-lagged.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:25.490
Could you give him a 
thirty-minute refresher course?

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:26.990
Sure thing.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:31.000
She's our promising junior, so go easy on her.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.290
<i>Her shots stretch really far.</i>

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:41.800
<i>How can she hit so hard 
with such a slender body?</i>

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:43.590
Sorry!

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:45.840
<i>But it feels a little rough.</i>

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:52.230
<i>Maybe her personality is a little rough, too...</i>

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:00.810
<i>She's getting more and more annoyed!</i>

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.570
<i>It's not my fault, is it?</i>

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:06.150
<i>Still...</i>

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:08.990
<i>I was nervous because she's 
their "promising junior,"</i>

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:11.900
<i>but it doesn't feel too different 
from the junior girls in Japan.</i>

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:17.080
<i>Just because it's America, it doesn't 
mean everyone's monstrously strong.</i>

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.080
All right, let's call it a day.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:21.090
Thanks, Marcia.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.910
Uh, um...

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:23.710
Thank you.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.400
You're not bad.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:28.870
That style of play must mean you're 
aiming for the French Open.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:29.390
Huh?

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.700
She's asking if you're aiming
for the French Open, because

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:36.140
the emphasis there is on stable play 
and not speed, unlike at Wimbledon.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.140
I've never even given it any thought.

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:42.070
I'm only thinking about the 
All-Japan Junior right now.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.570
All-Japan?

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:44.440
Yeah.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.100
I want to win the All-Japan Junior

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.270
and become a professional tennis player.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:52.330
It's the biggest tournament 
among the juniors in Japan.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.160
How small.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.210
Huh?!

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:58.130
If that's all it takes to be a pro in Japan,

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:00.670
I wish you'd take my brother there with you.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.840
Was she... making fun of me?

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:10.550
She said you were small!

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:11.180
Crush

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.850
Her brother just recently became a pro.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:17.550
But he's struggling, and it bothers her.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:19.760
Marcia's got a mouth on her,

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:22.620
but she's not a bad girl at heart, 
so forgive her, okay?

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:23.860
Right...

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.150
Now, let me show you to the dorm.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:29.860
Time to dig in—

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:34.240
Don't tell anyone about this, okay, Krishna?

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:36.290
Here it is!

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:41.170
H-Hi, Mike!

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:44.670
This is Maruo Eiichiro-kun. 
He'll be staying here for two weeks.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:46.920
Um, nice to meet you.

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:48.200
Likewise!

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:51.480
Atsushi, he's Japanese like you.

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:53.360
Teach him a thing or two, will you?

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:54.870
All right, Mike.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:57.060
However...

00:06:58.130 --> 00:06:59.810
Don't teach him stuff like this.

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:01.820
Sorry.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:04.630
Why don't you bring him with you for dinner?

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:07.150
What?

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:10.090
This is the only place where we're allowed to eat?

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:10.900
That's right.

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:13.320
The menu's pretty substantial.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:14.410
Yeah...

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:17.910
But when you've been here 
for six months, like me...

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:22.090
You get tired of having nothing but 
vegetables, white fish, and chicken.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.960
Sometimes, you crave a huge burger.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:31.430
So even the food is taken care of for the players.

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:35.370
Eating with another Japanese 
person is nice, though.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:37.940
It makes me want to eat natto...

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:43.070
Anyway, if there's anything you 
don't understand, you can ask me.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:43.910
Thanks.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.250
Looks like everyone's here.

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:49.990
Well, then.

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:51.490
I'll introduce you.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.960
First, I'm Taira Atsushi. I'm nineteen.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:58.010
I'm aiming to become a pro 
while going to school here.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:00.870
This is Krishna. He's sixteen.

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:04.080
It's been about a year since 
you came from India, right?

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.370
This is Alex, who's the same age as me.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:10.300
He's not in school anymore, 
so he's a pro player.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:12.880
He's ranked 819th in the world.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:15.720
<i>A professional player...</i>

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:18.160
Introduce yourself, Maruo-kun.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.530
Oh, yeah.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:22.200
I'm Maruo Eiichiro.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.790
I'm from Japan.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:25.020
I'm seventeen.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.830
I'm looking to go pro.

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:29.150
It's nice to meet you.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:32.690
Are you the one Mike brought over?

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:33.240
Huh?

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.430
I think my little sister said 
something rude to you.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:37.370
Sorry about that.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.570
You met Marcia?

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:40.790
Marcia...

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:44.620
<i>So her brother is...</i>

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.270
<i>They look alike.</i>

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:50.120
Uh, no, it didn't bother me at all.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.800
It's okay!

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.790
All right, let's go to bed!

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:56.740
We gotta get up early again tomorrow.

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:59.030
Oh, Maruo-kun, your bed is above mine.

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:00.470
Oh, all right.

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:19.910
<i>Jet lag?</i>

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:21.200
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.080
<i>I'm just worked up.</i>

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:27.460
<i>My training in America finally starts tomorrow.</i>

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:29.970
<i>There's no time to be nervous.</i>

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:31.210
<i>I have to get some sleep!</i>

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:34.010
Eiichiro went to Florida?!

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:36.430
It's only a two-week exchange program.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.610
I bet he's panicking.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:41.810
Hopefully he won't get homesick.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:43.220
He'll be fine.

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:44.580
But, Nat-chan,

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:47.970
the environment is completely 
different overseas, isn't it?

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:49.890
That's true, but...

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:51.320
I bet he's fine.

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:54.280
He's bolder than he looks, after all.

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:56.990
Bro is just passionate about training!

00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:02.160
Imagine how it feels to be the one 
forced to accompany him in that training!

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.780
<i>So-chan, I need a favor.</i>

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:11.040
<i>Ei-chan is over there, and...</i>

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:15.190
<i>We get up at 5:30.</i>

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:16.230
Good morning.

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:17.050
Did you sleep well?

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:18.950
Oh... Yes.

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:20.590
Are you hungry?

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:22.180
Yeah, somewhat.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:24.020
Well, let's eat.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:25.430
This seat taken?

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:26.850
Ike-kun!

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:28.510
Hey, Maruo-kun!

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:29.980
So you made it.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:33.640
You know Ike-kun?

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:34.480
Yes.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:37.110
I'm in the same club Ike-kun was in.

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:39.130
We played a match together once.

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:41.780
Speaking of that, you remember, don't you?

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.870
That you owe me for that point.

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:45.990
Owe you...

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.010
<i>Oh, that?</i>

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:50.040
<i>I wonder if he's the type to hold a grudge...</i>

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:53.050
Maybe I'll have you pay 
that off while you're here.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.800
He's tight with Soji, huh?

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:58.920
<i>He got to play a match against 
a top pro like Ike-kun...</i>

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:01.640
<i>Does that mean he's actually really good?</i>

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:04.640
<i>Warm-up starts at 7:00.</i>

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:06.140
<i>Then, at 8:00...</i>

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.400
<i>Finally...</i>

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:08.580
Hey!

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.770
See you in the meeting room at 8:00.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:13.650
Huh? We're not going to practice?

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:19.990
Here, this one's for you.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.160
Level 1~5
Sleep Duration
Sleep Quality
Food Amount
Food Quality
Motivation

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.160
Weight

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.160
Aches or Strains

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:25.340
What is this?

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:30.120
Every day, players here take notes on 
their eating habits, sleeping habits,

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:35.230
and their body's condition, focusing on 
awareness of their instinctual needs.

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:36.360
Instinctual...

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:39.380
This gives the coaches a better 
understanding of the players.

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:43.120
We start practice after working together 
to determine each player's goal.

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:46.140
My coach in Japan said the same thing.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:48.380
Here, fill yours out.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.220
<i>First, I need to listen to my instinct.</i>

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:58.400
Motivation

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:03.780
Wow, they're good.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:07.990
This class is for new pro players and 
those who want to be pro players.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.160
Everyone above this level practices individually.

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:14.040
They hire multiple coaches and trainers

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:17.430
with the money they bring in 
from tournaments and contracts.

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:20.050
They're basically tournament pros like Ike Soji.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:22.330
But,

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:25.310
all the pros here are just 
scraping by due to the cost

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:26.890
of lessons and living expenses.

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:29.370
We're all part of the same institution,

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:32.140
but the difference between us 
and pros is like night and day.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:33.390
Next!

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:34.260
Right!

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:35.400
Good luck.

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:47.410
All right, let's take a short break.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:53.410
<i>Practice isn't that different 
from what we did in Japan.</i>

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:54.480
Ei-chan!

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.230
Do you have a minute?

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:57.460
What is it?

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:00.670
I wanted to show you something neat.

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:02.710
Something neat?

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:06.220
This is...

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:07.720
Me from just now?

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:10.220
When were these taken?

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:13.230
There are a few cameras courtside.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:17.480
This way, you can watch your play 
and check your form at any time.

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:19.540
And that's not all.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:21.400
If you have any questions about technique,

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:24.150
the skill coaches will answer them right away.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:28.080
We have a team of specialists 
in every aspect of tennis

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:32.240
who are always ready to assist you 
in achieving your aspirations.

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:35.750
It's up to you to decide how to make use of this.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:37.500
<i>Incredible...</i>

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:41.620
<i>Here, we wake up for tennis, eat for tennis...</i>

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:44.260
<i>Everything we see, hear, and talk about is tennis.</i>

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:48.760
<i>This might truly be a place where 
you can live solely for tennis.</i>

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:53.310
If you want to improve at tennis, there's 
no better environment than this, is there?

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:57.540
I saw Ike-kun's pro debut game in Japan.

00:13:58.090 --> 00:14:01.310
I was so envious of Ike-kun going pro.

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:02.730
I thought to myself,

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:06.820
it must be nice to live solely for tennis every day.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.250
And here...

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:11.090
I might be able to have that.

00:14:17.030 --> 00:14:20.580
Today, the twenty of us are going to be 
divided into four brackets for matches.

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:25.340
We observe each match and do some 
mental training while we await our turns.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:28.690
On weekday afternoons, we go over 
what we learned in the match

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:31.740
and end the day with practice.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:34.500
And there are usually some matches 
over the weekend on some other courts,

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:37.100
so we sometimes participate in those...

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:39.930
What have you been writing?

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:40.520
Huh?

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:43.020
Tennis 40

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:43.020
This is my tennis notebook.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:44.910
Tennis notebook?

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:46.180
Let me take a look.

00:14:46.180 --> 00:14:48.470
Oh, then have this one.

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:50.530
Here.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.550
Tennis 38

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:54.600
Wow.

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:58.580
Your handwriting is so neat.

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:01.160
But what are you doing this for?

00:15:01.160 --> 00:15:03.220
It's to make sure I don't forget what I learned,

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:04.920
and so I can refer back to the match—

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:04.920
Hang on!

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:06.640
How many of those do you have?!

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:09.420
This is my fortieth one...

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:10.860
What the heck?

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:14.100
Wow! I heard the Japanese are diligent.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:15.400
I guess it's true.

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:17.180
No, no, no! Not all of us are like this!

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:18.640
Be quiet!

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:20.390
Observing the match is also part of practice.

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:22.400
We're sorry!

00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:24.180
<i>That's right.</i>

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:26.810
<i>Even if this is the best environment,</i>

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:28.900
<i>I'm here for only two weeks.</i>

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:32.410
<i>What I lack in particular is actual experience.</i>

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:37.380
<i>That's exactly why I want to play as many 
matches against good players as possible.</i>

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:38.200
Next!

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:40.330
Maruo and Alex, get in!

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:42.050
It's your turn.

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:42.680
Yeah.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:46.380
<i>I'm up against Alex... Which means...</i>

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:47.900
<i>A match against a pro!</i>

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:51.130
Huh?

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:58.290
I want an opponent other than Maruo.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.150
What?!

00:15:59.150 --> 00:15:59.890
Why?

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:01.670
I'm a pro.

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:04.520
I'd like to play against someone on my own level.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:06.020
But...

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:10.150
He went pro just recently, so he must be on edge.

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:11.610
But I can—

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:13.840
There aren't any pros here.

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:15.720
I saw Soji earlier.

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:17.180
Isn't he available?

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:17.950
I don't know.

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:19.270
I guess we can ask.

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:20.160
U-Um...

00:16:19.270 --> 00:16:21.330
It looked like Soji went to the practice courts.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:24.750
Um, instead of Ike-kun, I'd like—

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:25.390
You called?

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:27.520
Ike-kun?!

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:28.090
Yo.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.760
Hey, Soji.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:32.650
Would you mind playing a match with Alex?

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:36.660
Um, but Coach, at first you said 
that Alex and I would have a match...

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:38.350
So, I mean, uh...

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.990
I see.

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:41.410
So that's it.

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:44.890
That's fine. I'll do it.

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:45.600
What?!

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:46.820
You don't mind?

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:47.610
Thanks.

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:50.610
Wha... Um, wait...

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:50.610
Wait a second.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:53.290
I want a match against Soji, too!

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:54.240
Me, too.

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:55.030
Me, too!

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:55.610
What?!

00:16:56.150 --> 00:16:59.890
It's not often you get to face a 
top-ranked tournament pro in a match!

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:01.760
I-Is that right?

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:03.160
<i>Wait a second...</i>

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:04.620
<i>What about me?</i>

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:07.710
Man, I sure am popular!

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:10.980
Hmm... But it's not like I can 
play this many matches in a day...

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:15.160
And I want to face someone good enough 
to be useful for my training, too...

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:16.630
What about...

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:19.260
All right!

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:25.810
I'll play against whoever beats Maruo-kun.

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:27.140
Huh?

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.270
Me?!

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:36.280
U-Uh, why me?

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.130
What's the problem?

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:41.120
I'll face you if you can defeat anyone here.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:45.180
And I'll face the person who can defeat Maruo-kun

00:17:45.180 --> 00:17:46.870
sometime during his two weeks here.

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:51.430
If it means I can have a match with 
Soji, I'll play against Maruo now.

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:54.260
Are you telling me he's that good?

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:56.150
I dunno.

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:56.880
Huh?

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:00.890
But he probably won't let you win so easily.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:03.140
So you do have a high opinion of him.

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:07.390
I'll be training, so come get me 
when you figure out my opponent.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:08.380
All right.

00:18:10.410 --> 00:18:11.290
Do your best.

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:18.530
<i>Is this...</i>

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:21.110
<i>an opportunity Ike-kun created for me?!</i>

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:23.490
<i>Thank you, Ike-kun!</i>

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:25.200
Well, let's get started, then.

00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:28.040
Y-Yeah!

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:30.330
Huh?

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:33.920
Alex and Eiichiro?

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:36.920
Looks like they're gonna have a match.

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:40.930
Sender: Natsu
Add: Ike Soji
Ei-chan
So when Ei-chan gets over there, 
help him out, will you?
I think he'll get a lot better.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:43.240
<i>Since Natsu asked me to, 
I gave you an opportunity.</i>

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:46.380
<i>But the rest is up to you,</i>

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:47.690
<i>Maruo-kun.</i>

00:18:56.460 --> 00:19:01.110
<i>The reason I rejected a match against you 
isn't just because you're an amateur.</i>

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:06.380
<i>It's also because most players that come 
from Asia don't understand Western etiquette.</i>

00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:11.620
<i>A notebook?</i>

00:19:11.990 --> 00:19:14.540
Eiichiro is doing something weird.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.440
He's really taking notes.

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:18.630
He uses that even during matches, I guess.

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:21.650
<i>My attack pattern has three steps.</i>

00:19:21.650 --> 00:19:24.040
<i>First, I rally to get a feel for the opponent.</i>

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:25.990
<i>Second, if I can, I go for a winner.</i>

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:27.810
<i>Even if I can't, I advance forward.</i>

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:30.390
<i>Third, I go for the winner at net.</i>

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:33.870
<i>But he won't let me do this at all!</i>

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:36.900
<i>It's because he goes in for 
an attack during the rally.</i>

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:39.070
<i>But I'm starting to understand his tendencies.</i>

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:43.160
<i>Basically, all of his shots are low-risk.</i>

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.870
<i>He practically never comes 
forward for a high-risk shot.</i>

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:49.620
<i>Instead, he hits from the back and 
tries to win the point from his first shot.</i>

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:53.290
<i>He only comes forward when 
he knows he can win the point.</i>

00:19:53.770 --> 00:20:02.050
3) Go in for the score
2) If possible, take a shot
1) Observe

00:19:53.770 --> 00:20:02.050
2) Go in for the score
1) If possible, take a shot

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:58.330
<i>Compared to my attack pattern, he doesn't do step one, where he observes my play.</i>

00:19:58.330 --> 00:20:01.550
<i>That's why the rhythm feels fast 
and therefore hard to deal with.</i>

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:06.540
<i>Always being on the offensive is pretty crazy.</i>

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:09.830
<i>If I consider all of his shots 
to be potential winners,</i>

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:11.480
<i>his style doesn't seem so rough.</i>

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:12.060
Time!

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:16.560
<i>It takes me three steps to win 
a point, and only two for Alex.</i>

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:20.320
<i>What do I do to make up the difference?</i>

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.320
<i>If you need two steps...</i>

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:24.570
<i>Then I'll go after you</i>

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:25.490
<i>in fewer!</i>

00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:29.080
<i>If I serve and volley, it's just one step!</i>

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:31.980
Ah...

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:33.790
Love-15.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:34.740
Lame.

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:36.000
With a serve like that...

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:39.050
<i>That was way too reckless.</i>

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:41.050
He's changing his attack pattern.

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:42.550
<i>If that's the case...</i>

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:44.490
<i>What can I do?</i>

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:52.060
<i>I'll use my 1/64 control, 
and go for the win from the start!</i>

00:20:54.290 --> 00:20:55.210
Out!

00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:56.560
Love-30.

00:20:56.990 --> 00:20:59.770
<i>The ball is too heavy! I can't control it!</i>

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:02.740
<i>Defense only?!</i>

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:06.110
Game: Alex. 4-0.

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:07.950
Good job, Alex!

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:11.450
<i>If I could just get used to the rhythm, 
I feel like I could handle this...</i>

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:13.450
5-0.

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:19.520
<i>But before that, I have to 
get used to these heavy shots.</i>

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:28.510
Game, set.

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:31.510
Winner: Alex. Score: 6-0.

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:35.410
<i>I can't even make a dent...</i>

00:21:35.970 --> 00:21:37.720
<i>This type of tennis exists?!</i>

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:42.600
Soji.

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:45.530
I won against Maruo.

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:47.060
That was quick!

00:21:47.060 --> 00:21:48.090
What was the score?

00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:49.080
6-0.

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:51.910
I see.

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:53.540
Well, that sounds about right.

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:55.120
Got it.

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.100
Let's start when you're ready.

00:21:57.100 --> 00:21:58.320
Wait a second, Soji.

00:21:59.320 --> 00:22:01.420
Why did you say that earlier?

00:22:02.030 --> 00:22:04.480
That Maruo wouldn't let me win so easily.

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:06.170
I just felt that way.

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:10.350
He's only been playing tennis 
for two years, you know.

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:11.130
What?

00:22:11.590 --> 00:22:13.920
He started in the spring when he was fifteen.

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:16.250
Don't you think that's amazing?

00:22:17.300 --> 00:22:19.410
It hasn't even been two years?

00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:26.800
<i>This is the world's standard for tennis...</i>

00:22:28.240 --> 00:22:29.990
<i>I have to think of a strategy!</i>

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.850 --> 00:24:01.930
Marcia?!

00:24:02.430 --> 00:24:04.000
I don't get it!

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:08.000
Why are you writing down your losing 
score and ball movements so precisely?

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:08.430
Huh?

00:24:08.430 --> 00:24:09.460
And what the heck?

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:11.720
Aren't you frustrated about 
losing against my brother?

00:24:11.720 --> 00:24:13.760
Why do you look so satisfied?!

00:24:13.760 --> 00:24:18.300
O-Of course I'm frustrated, but I'm happy 
I got to play against someone good.

00:24:18.300 --> 00:24:19.890
What a weirdo.

00:24:20.210 --> 00:24:22.230
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>:

00:24:21.790 --> 00:24:25.020
A Vicious Circle is Lucky

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:24.010
"A Vicious Circle is Lucky."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:31.000
End
